  "text": "Recipe: Grilled Pizza Sandwich\nCreator: Padma Subramanian\nCategory: Sandwich\nIngredients: 4 leftover oil free phulkas (can sub with WFPB tortillas), Cucumbers sliced, Onions thinly sliced, Beets thinly sliced, Tomatoes thinly sliced, Chaat Masala, Sanchal (kala namak | black salt), 1/2 cup Green Teekhi Chaat Ki Chutney, Homemade Tomato Ketchup (WFPB)\nCooking methods: no-cook, grill\nInstructions: Spread the chutney on phulkas. Make a slit so that it goes through to half the phulka's diameter. In one quarter, keep cucumber slices. In the second quarter, beet slices. In the third quarter, onion slices and last quarter tomato slices. Sprinkle some Chaat Masala and sanchal on top.\nFold the roti into quarter starting from the slit folding over each type of veggie.\nPut it in a hot pre seasoned cast iron pan or non stick grill and grill until crisp.\nTop with WFPB tomato ketchup and enjoy.\nNotes: Green Teekhi Chaat Ki Chutney, Homemade Tomato Ketchup (WFPB)",
